# Claude Code settings (local only)
.claude/

# Un-ignore .mcp.json. The GLOBAL excludes file
# (C:/Users/danie/.gitignore_global:3) lists `.mcp.json`, which is correct for
# a local Claude Code client config but wrong here, where .mcp.json IS the
# plugin's MCP server manifest and must ship. A repo-level negation overrides
# the global rule without changing machine-wide behaviour for other repos.
!.mcp.json

# NOTE: .mcp.json is deliberately NOT ignored.
# It was ignored here until 2026-08-04, which silently broke this repo as a
# Claude Code plugin: .mcp.json is the plugin's MCP server manifest, so the
# marketplace clone had no server config and the server could never start.
# The failure was invisible locally -- the file exists on disk, so every local
# test passed -- and `git add` skipped it without comment on every commit.
# If it ever needs to be local-only again, the plugin packaging has to change too.

