# Compiled executables (Bun compiled, ~95MB each).
#
# This rule and the repo contents used to contradict each other: `*.exe` was
# ignored while three binaries totalling 166 MB were tracked anyway (ignore
# rules do not apply to already-tracked files). Resolved 2026-08-07:
#
#   - create-dependency-graph.exe is NO LONGER tracked. It is the only one that
#     grows -- every rebuild adds ~95 MB to history permanently -- and it is not
#     needed for the supported path, since `npm run docs:deps` runs the .ts via
#     tsx. It had also drifted 8 months behind its source and would have
#     silently generated stale output. It ships as a GitHub release asset, and
#     `npm run build` in its directory rebuilds it. Its old blobs remain in
#     history; nothing was destroyed.
#   - chunking-for-files.exe and compress-for-context.exe REMAIN tracked. They
#     have not changed since 2025-12-24, so they accumulate nothing, and
#     untracking them would remove working tooling from a fresh clone for no
#     benefit.
*.exe
/output
/.claude
.claude/settings.local.json
# Added by post-migration audit (2026-05-01)
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
memory.db
memory.db.backup.*

# npm auth. Publishing is done locally and needs an .npmrc holding
# `//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}` -- a variable REFERENCE, never
# the token itself. Ignored so neither the reference nor an accidental literal
# can be committed.
.npmrc
